{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_FRTP_SECTION_7_5_1_1_TX_SDU_AVAILABLE","src":"manifest","doc":"SWS_FlexRayISOTransportLayer","page":40,"text":"7.5.1.1 TX_SDU_AVAILABLE\nThe TX_SDU_AVAILABLE flag is set by the service primitive FrTp_Transmit to indi-\ncate the N-SDU transmit request.\n[SWS_FrTp_00415]\nA\nTX\nSDU\navailable\nflag\nper\nchannel\n⌈The\nTX_SDU_AVAILABLE flag shall exist for every channel.⌋\n[SWS_FrTp_00416] TX SDU available flag use case ⌈The TX_SDU_AVAILABLE flag\nshall indicate an Fr N-SDU transmit request for a configured connection on an allocated\nchannel.⌋\nNote: For detailed information about set and reset conditions and behaviour please\nrefer to Section 7.5.2 and [SWS_FrTp_01057].","caption":"7.5.1.1 TX_SDU_AVAILABLE","sha":null,"series":[{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_FRTP_SECTION_7_5_1_1_TX_SDU_AVAILABLE","releases":["R23-11"],"page":42,"hash":"8726c97a86bc97e2","caption":""},{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_FRTP_SECTION_7_5_1_1_TX_SDU_AVAILABLE","releases":["R24-11"],"page":40,"hash":"55cc52443e72b28f","caption":""}],"releases":["R23-11","R24-11"],"kind":"snippet","platform":"classic","targets":[{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_FrTp_00415] im Text von SWS_FlexRayISOTransportLayer.","rel":["R24-11"],"id":"SWS_FrTp_00415"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_FrTp_00416] im Text von SWS_FlexRayISOTransportLayer.","rel":["R24-11"],"id":"SWS_FrTp_00416"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_FrTp_01057] im Text von SWS_FlexRayISOTransportLayer.","rel":["R24-11"],"id":"SWS_FrTp_01057"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.85,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Signaling ongoing transfer via TX_SDU_AVAILABLE","rel":[],"id":"SWS_FrTp_01038"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.85,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Setting conditions for TX_SDU_AVAILABLE","rel":[],"id":"SWS_FrTp_01039"}],"ok":true,"schema":"versions-explorer@1"}